Body:
Measured on Qwen3.8-27B/vLLM/Intel B70:

- normal request: 180,980 tokens; 176,000 cached
- compaction: 137,459 input; 0 cached; 443.031 seconds

The shared request builder is the right approach IMO. Suggestions before merge:

- make it opt-in; keep #40800 serialization as fallback;
- preserve the triggering request's agent, variant, user system, tool filters, system, tools, and typed prefix;
- set `toolChoice: "none"` while retaining tools; vLLM retains them unless started with `--exclude-tools-when-tool-choice-none`;
- fall back for overflow, unsafe splits, prior compaction, media, and non-OpenAI-compatible providers;
- test canonical prefix equality and unchanged default behavior.

Currently, `active` comes from `selected.head`. A later user may have changed the variant, user system, or tool filters, so prefix identity is not guaranteed. Enabling this for every provider may also reintroduce #40800.

Review: GPT-5.6-sol and Claude Opus 5.
